1
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:35,337
I'll see you

2
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:40,400
next time.

3
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,577
When the ocean started to disappear,

4
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:02,072
we took it as a sign that
things might get back to normal.

5
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:04,417
The odds of that happening anytime soon?

6
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,480
Not good.

7
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:17,090
Matt!

8
00:02:17,173 --> 00:02:18,003
Hey, Matt!

9
00:02:18,086 --> 00:02:19,680
Matt, where are you?

10
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:22,040
I'm worried.

11
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:24,337
What do you think could
have happened to him, Tai?

12
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:25,357
Matt's a big boy.

13
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,797
He could take care of himself.

14
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:27,797
Well, wait a minute.

15
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:29,937
What if he was kidnapped by Puppet Mod?

16
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,477
Yeah, he might have been.

17
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:32,700
Or something worse.

18
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:36,040
No, it wasn't anything like that.

19
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:37,660
Huh? What?

20
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:38,940
How do you know?

21
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:42,000
Come on, let's go. Huh?

22
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:44,120
What, he just walked away?

23
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:47,900
And you didn't even try
to stop him? Well, no.

24
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:49,177
Was I supposed to?

25
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:51,457
I mean, I thought he was
just gonna go use the bushes.

26
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:52,380
Or something.

27
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:53,990
Huh.

28
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:55,477
This is weird.

29
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,697
I mean, it's one thing
if he was kidnapped,

30
00:02:57,780 --> 00:02:59,877
but why would he just
disappear on us like this?

31
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:00,790
I'll say.

32
00:03:00,873 --> 00:03:03,057
He's been gone way too long
for just a potty break.

33
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:03,970
Wait a minute.

34
00:03:04,053 --> 00:03:06,917
Is it just me, or has Matt
been kind of strange lately?

35
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,294
He has been acting a little hot streak.

36
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:12,997
Remember when Gabumon had
that digivolving problem?

37
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:15,021
Yeah, I bet there's a connection.

38
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,320
Kari, what is it?

39
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:21,337
I thought I heard a voice out there.

40
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:22,660
A voice? Was it Matt?

41
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:24,570
What?

42
00:03:24,653 --> 00:03:25,483
I don't hear anything.

43
00:03:25,566 --> 00:03:28,086
Come on, Kari, don't you
start losing it, too.

44
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:31,357
He couldn't be very far away, you know.

45
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:32,817
Maybe we should look for him.

46
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:33,841
Yeah, I suppose.

47
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,235
Okay, guys, let's go.

48
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:43,577
Gatomon, it wasn't Matt's voice I heard.

49
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:44,680
Whose was it?

50
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,620
Matt, come on.

51
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:52,802
I'm all for exercise, but I'm
really not built for long distances.

52
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,560
Matt, where are we going? Just away.

53
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:57,020
I need some space.

54
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:01,060
Oh, the poor little kid
needs a little space.

55
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:05,217
Someplace far away from his nice
little friends and closer than me.

56
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,000
I agree completely.

57
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:08,380
I'm not waiting.

58
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:10,177
I'll put him out of his misery.

59
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,357
Those Digi-Dustin' kids really bug me.

60
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,777
Wait a minute, Puppetmon.

61
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:15,320
I have a better idea.

62
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:21,137
You can take care of those other
Digi-Dustin' children if you want to,

63
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:23,396
But as for this one, leave him to me.

64
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:27,088
I'll have him climbing up a tree
before I'm through with him.

65
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:32,451
You ever felt like a fifth wheel, Gabumon?

66
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,052
That's what I feel like.

67
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:39,260
All this time, I thought I
had like a purpose, you know?

68
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:41,600
To look out for my little brother.

69
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:46,077
I thought TK wouldn't be able to
survive without me watching over him.

70
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:48,820
But suddenly, it's like he's growing up.

71
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:50,808
He doesn't need me anymore.

72
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:53,080
Oh, and it's not just him.

73
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,160
It's everybody, man.

74
00:04:56,800 --> 00:05:00,360
I mean, when I think of Tai and
Mimi and Sora and the others,

75
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:03,497
this place has changed
them for the better.

76
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:04,815
They're stronger now.

77
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:08,122
It's almost like they've
digivolved or something.

78
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:10,860
But you see, the problem is, I haven't.

79
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:13,240
I'm still stuck in the same place.

80
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,900
I haven't changed a bit.

81
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:18,080
You may not see it, Matt,
but you've changed a lot.

82
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:20,397
Oh, please, Gabumon, give me a break.

83
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:22,760
I'm the same jerk I always was.

84
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:23,980
Hey, come on.

85
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:25,600
It'll never happen.

86
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:26,720
Not this way.

87
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,840
I finally got it figured out.

88
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:31,897
If I'm ever going to change,
I have to do it on my own.

89
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:33,060
On my own.

90
00:05:33,860 --> 00:05:35,420
The others can't help me.

91
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,640
Well, well, well.

92
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,380
Look what we've got here.

93
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:42,251
Greetings, nature lovers.

94
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,350
What?

95
00:05:45,433 --> 00:05:47,811
You mean you've never seen a talking tree?

96
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,020
Not many.

97
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:50,380
Be careful.

98
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,457
That's Cherry Mod, Lord of the Forest,

99
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:55,481
and the best reason for
the existence of termites.

100
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,557
Stop right there or I'll
turn you into toothpicks.

101
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:01,640
You really shouldn't be that rude.

102
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,630
Calm down.

103
00:06:02,713 --> 00:06:03,917
My fighting days are over.

104
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,706
I only want to talk with you.

105
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:09,620
In fact, you might even say
I've turned over a new leaf.

106
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:14,880
It's no use.

107
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:16,236
I'm getting nothing.

108
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:19,737
For some reason, the digivices
aren't working in this forest.

109
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:23,232
You know, I'm not so sure we
should be trying to find him.

110
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,217
Everyone needs to be alone sometimes.

111
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:26,130
I should know.

112
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:28,177
I'm not gonna let him break up this team.

113
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:30,677
We're gonna find him whether
he wants us to or not.

114
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,917
We're always walking around
searching for someone.

115
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,797
I've never done so much
walking in my life.

116
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,174
Yeah, it's disgusting.

117
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,037
My calves are starting to
look like a bodybuilder's.

118
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:42,380
Like a what? Oh, Mimi. Yoo-hoo! Huh?

119
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:44,270
Puppet Mod!

120
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:46,380
Hi, everybody.

121
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:48,297
Hey, TK, did you miss me?

122
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:52,097
No, not at all, and I'm not going
to play with you anymore, either.

123
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:53,010
No?

124
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:54,620
Well, fine.

125
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:56,497
You're not a lot of fun anyway.

126
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,227
Front and center, everybody.

127
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:04,260
Oh, Garbagemon, they're
as tough as they are mean.

128
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:06,854
And they don't smell very good, either.

129
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:09,420
Dunk Tuckers ready, aim, fire!

130
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:16,930
Mimi!

131
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,200
I won't budge!

132
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,849
Let's let them do the
running for a change!

133
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:30,260
Mimi, come on!

134
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:31,361
Yeah, good idea.

135
00:07:31,620 --> 00:07:32,617
I must be nuts!

136
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:33,935
I touched that stuff!

137
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:40,420
No offense, but even if I felt like
talking, it wouldn't be to a tree.

138
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:41,802
See you around.

139
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:45,177
Hey, what's the idea?

140
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:49,417
Young man, didn't anyone ever tell
you you should listen to your elders?

141
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:51,417
Or was it Redwood you should listen to?

142
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,697
I can never quite get those two straight.

143
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:55,074
But anyway, I digress.

144
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:57,992
So, you're still stuck in the same place.

145
00:07:58,560 --> 00:08:00,913
Still the same old jerk you always were.

146
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:02,557
Surprised, huh?

147
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:04,000
I know all about it.

148
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:06,220
Must be tough being in such a rut.

149
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:08,125
You've been spying on me, huh?

150
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:11,040
Listen to me, kid.

151
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:13,477
I don't need to spy because
there's nothing that

152
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:16,017
happens in this forest
that I don't know about.

153
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:16,930
Huh.

154
00:08:17,013 --> 00:08:17,843
All right, then.

155
00:08:17,926 --> 00:08:19,577
If you're so smart, what
am I supposed to do?

156
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:20,490
Tell me that.

157
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:22,040
Ah, simple as that, eh?

158
00:08:22,780 --> 00:08:27,020
Kids, you want all the answers just
handed to you on a mahogany platter.

159
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:29,557
But you never want to do
the hard work of looking

160
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:32,840
deep within yourself where
all the answers truly lie.

161
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:34,500
Let's go.

162
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:37,337
Don't you listen to that
talking firewood, Matt.

163
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:38,250
Come on.

164
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,420
That's right. Go on.

165
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:44,100
But you'll never learn how to change.

166
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:46,853
You'll always be what you are right now.

167
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:48,360
I want to change.

168
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:51,037
Yes, of course, but are you really ready?

169
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,237
After all, change isn't
always a pleasant thing.

170
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:55,817
You might find out a few things
that you wish you hadn't.

171
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:56,730
I'm ready.

172
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:58,521
More than ready.

173
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:00,952
Enough talking, big guy.

174
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,417
If you've got some answers, let's see him.

175
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:05,720
He fell for it like an overripe fig.

176
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:08,620
All right, kid, I'll help you out.

177
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:12,517
First off, you're going to
have to defeat your rival.

178
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,500
My rival?

179
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,620
There, in that lake,

180
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:18,857
you will see the face of
the one who is preventing

181
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:21,580
you from becoming as
strong as you could be.

182
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:24,156
Where are you going?

183
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:27,596
I know it sounds pretty
bogus, but might as well look.

184
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:29,770
Listen, Matt.

185
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:33,096
You don't really believe him, do you?

186
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:45,520
Tai, come on!

187
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:47,860
What kind of trick is this?

188
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:09,650
Ah!

189
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:13,277
Don't you know that wherever you
go, there will always be garbage!

190
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:15,980
Okay, ready guys? Make a mess!

191
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:26,880
Meteor away!

192
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:29,600
An electro shocker!

193
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,277
Our full torpedoes!

194
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,480
You're getting way for Nino-Spotty!

195
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:35,520
Nova Blast!

196
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,280
Way to go!

197
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:47,380
That trash is thrashed!

198
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:52,380
Wait, you've totally
ruined my garbage fun!

199
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,108
I'm beaten, I'm going home!

200
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,030
Psych!

201
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:55,943
Look behind you!

202
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:58,520
Oh, no! Help!

203
00:10:59,140 --> 00:10:59,970
Juntaker!

204
00:11:00,053 --> 00:11:01,600
Nightmare!

205
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:30,770
Lillymon!

206
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:34,630
Kijimon?

207
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:42,260
Twash is nice!

208
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:47,272
Trash that for too dumb!

209
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:52,860
That chick is heavier than C-Buck.

210
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:56,300
Flower, get it!

211
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:02,360
All right, finish him off!

212
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:52,000
Behold the face of your rival so you're
saying I have to fight tie is that it

213
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:59,787
nice dry foliage face yeah I'd be going
there we'll have to do better than that

214
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:03,397
I had nothing to do with it.

215
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:06,917
The lake of truth reflects only what
is in a person's heart, hence the name.

216
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,471
You've got to be kidding.

217
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:09,830
Sorry, kid.

218
00:13:09,913 --> 00:13:10,743
It's never wrong.

219
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:13,090
That right?

220
00:13:13,173 --> 00:13:14,217
Well, I've got news for you.

221
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:15,960
It's off this time. Way off.

222
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:18,037
Well, you can argue with me all you want,

223
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:20,767
but you're really only
arguing with yourself.

224
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:22,890
Huh.

225
00:13:22,973 --> 00:13:24,977
It's about time you face the truth.

226
00:13:25,060 --> 00:13:26,857
The one you call Tai is your leader.

227
00:13:26,940 --> 00:13:27,857
Everything he says you do.

228
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:29,297
Everywhere he goes, you follow,

229
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:31,357
and yet in your heart you
resent it because you know

230
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:34,322
you're just as qualified
to be the boss as he is.

231
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:37,270
Stop it!

232
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:40,240
Who do you think you are? Huh?

233
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:42,857
Who died and left you
in charge of the world?

234
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:43,770
Huh?

235
00:13:43,853 --> 00:13:44,683
What do you mean?

236
00:13:44,766 --> 00:13:45,596
I've just about had it.

237
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:49,060
Do not be ashamed of your
resentment. Do not hide it.

238
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:52,340
Embrace it, for in your
anger lies your strength.

239
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:57,400
Only when you recognize that will you
at last be free to grow, to change.

240
00:13:57,940 --> 00:14:03,520
So face your rival and prove you are
his equal, or better, by defeating him.

241
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:05,650
Don't listen.

242
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:07,517
He's just trying to cause trouble.

243
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:09,600
He's playing games with your mind.

244
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:11,697
It's all part of some kind of trap.

245
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:12,839
Tai is your friend.

246
00:14:13,380 --> 00:14:14,700
He's my friend, yeah.

247
00:14:15,780 --> 00:14:19,960
He may not always act like it,
but he's right. Ty's my friend.

248
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,826
You don't fight your friends.

249
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:23,980
Friend? Ha!

250
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:25,597
Now that's a good one.

251
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:28,057
You don't even believe that such a thing

252
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:31,440
really exists Not in your
heart of hearts anyway

253
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:37,320
Hit the nail on the head, didn't I?

254
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:38,902
What's he mean?

255
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:41,710
Friendship

256
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:43,070
Loyalty

257
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:44,630
Comrades

258
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:49,300
Fine-sounding words But
that's all they are Words

259
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:54,997
Delusions And you're wise enough
to see that now You'll know that

260
00:14:55,080 --> 00:15:00,280
ultimately The only person you can depend
on is yourself Isn't that right, Matt?

261
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:03,720
He's wrong, isn't he?

262
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:06,980
I don't know I don't know

263
00:15:07,700 --> 00:15:08,700
You don't?

264
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:13,340
All right, then That's enough
